-# ============================================================================
-# Pre-staged roadmap for 2026.06.352 (operator-staged, Claude Opus 4.8, 2026-06-04).
-#
-# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS / HOW IT ACTIVATES (Pre-Staged Roadmap Convention):
-#   The conductor preserves + auto-activates this file when the active milestone
-#   (.351) closes, because `milestone:` below == expected-next (.352). Until then
-#   it sits inert. The operator staged it; the planner is the fallback, not the default.
-#
-# PROVENANCE: the LDT + Huginn deep-read (2026-06-04), recorded in
-#   docs/research-notes/phase3-recursive-refiner-thesis.md and memory
-#   reference_tiny_recursive_reasoning_models.md. It re-frames the next recursive-
-#   refiner probe AWAY from re-reading HRM's continuous intermediate latents (which
-#   would only re-confirm the Deep-Think P3 negative that Huginn already gives us:
-#   recursive latents are non-decodable orbits) and TOWARD the one open question LDT
-#   leaves on the table.
-#
-# THE GAP THIS PROBES. LDT (arXiv:2605.08605) IS Carnot's transpilation+abstention
-#   thesis, built and SOTA — but ONLY for CLOSED grid domains with a HAND-BUILT
-#   abstract-interpretation lattice (per-cell candidate sets for Sudoku). Its power
-#   comes from two lattice properties: (1) SOUND elimination (it never eliminates a
-#   correct candidate) and (2) informative CONFLICT detection (it shrinks the wrong-
-#   candidate set). Carnot's differentiated bet is that a GENERAL multi-domain
-#   verifier ENSEMBLE (k=15) can serve as the abstraction lattice for OPEN-ENDED
-#   domains where no lattice can be hand-built. This task MEASURES whether the
-#   ensemble actually has LDT's two lattice properties on a non-grid domain
-#   (FoVer step-level math reasoning) — by re-scoring CACHED candidates. $0, CPU,
-#   no GPU, no generator training.
-#
-# WHY LOOP-SAFE: it is a PROPERTY MEASUREMENT, not a generation-beats-AR test, so
-#   there is NO baseline-to-beat and the headroom / FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK trap does
-#   not apply in the usual way — BUT a degenerate null (the ensemble eliminates
-#   nothing, or only by also eliminating correct answers) is still informative and
-#   is guarded by a random-elimination positive control at matched soundness.
-#   It re-scores cached artifacts (verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates
-#   substrate) so it dodges every GPU liability (kill_zombies / eGPU drop / pause).
-# ============================================================================
-
