-        0. PRECONDITIONS (blocked_* + EXIT if any fail):
-           a. `{project_root}/.venv/bin/python -c "import torch, numpy"` succeeds.
-           b. The exp3821 TRM checkpoint/source is loadable (read trm_checkpoint_source from its artifact);
-              if not, honest_verdict `blocked_trm_checkpoint_not_available`.
-        1. Load the trained TRM; run it on M >= 50 instances, capturing (h_t, Δh_t) pairs at every step.
-        2. Estimate the vector field's curl / Jacobian asymmetry directly: for the learned update map
-           F(h) = Δh, measure the antisymmetric part of its Jacobian (finite-diff or autograd) — a
-           conservative field has (near-)zero antisymmetric Jacobian / zero curl.
-        3. ALSO attempt a least-squares scalar-potential fit: parameterize E_φ(h), fit so that
-           −∇E_φ(h) ≈ F(h); report the residual ||F + ∇E_φ||/||F|| after convergence.
-        4. Compute a positive control: run the SAME pipeline on a KNOWN conservative field (e.g. an
-           actual EBT/Langevin update or a synthetic −∇E) — the fit MUST succeed there (residual ~0),
-           proving the test can detect conservativity when it exists.
-        5. Apply the gate -> terminal verdict.
-
